{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded","id":754554,"title":"Alien: the Stranded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T11:08:56-08:00","id":754554,"title":"Alien: the Stranded","content":"I've been watching this fan game for a little, it's Aliens in the World of Darkness. What's not to love? However, today I loaded it up and the owner had deleted it (and I don't know who the owner is) so I saved a copy here (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A5GWSFcHn1W55eJNXTcBiUNXek_AAMwsasrOjLvInZc/edit?copiedFromTrash#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...piedFromTrash#</a>) in case the owner frequents here, and can see that the work was saved, or if the owner keeps it deleted, so maybe it can be finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:20:34-08:00","id":754742,"title":"","content":"Not deleted...updated. Hold on a second I'll dig up the link that I updated in the OP...<br /> <br /> Use the following instead: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fPVMwMZdnrJZiJkUVIYKCHTQnfmq0fiLqUhlLBGif4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Got tired of working in Google Docs and switched to Word, which is what I write in natively (was copy and pasting from Word to Google before). No worries about finishing...although the manuscript is taking a wee bit longer than I anticipated. I think it (this rough draft) should be done around January~ish, at which time I'll be handing it off to the community here for edits and additional drafting so I can write another trashy novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":".  Updated this document again 08-06-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:31:35-08:00","id":754766,"title":"","content":"Ah, well man, I love your work. I got a little scared it got scrapped when I saw it was deleted. Thanks for replying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:40:38-08:00","id":754781,"title":"","content":"Thanks. No worries. Just needed to refresh the document. Made a global change to one term yesterday and didn't want to figure out how to repeat in Google Docs... so delete and new upload...<br /> <br /> This honestly argues that I should be doing stuff in Git but I'm not sure how Git and Word interact so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:13:47-08:00","id":756583,"title":"","content":"You mean native integration, or just how GIT might interact with a Word Doc? I haven't found any issues with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:21:23-08:00","id":767265,"title":"","content":"Noticed the other day that the original link was to the docx file and that updates weren't being reflected. Does anyone want to confirm that the new link actually links to a viewable version that reflects more recent updates?<br /> <br /> Repeating the link above down here for convenience: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fPVMwMZdnrJZiJkUVIYKCHTQnfmq0fiLqUhlLBGif4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Note that I haven't updated the original posts link (not sure that I want to go through that much thread necromancy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":".  Updated this document again. 08-06-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T09:52:01-08:00","id":771553,"title":"","content":"Can't say if the most recent updates are there, I didn't look this archive for quite some time by now, but it seems pretty long by now. I really wanted to take some more works going on that thread, but your Stranded was the one a looked forward most to see complete. It would be really a shame if it got lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:48:35-08:00","id":785497,"title":"","content":"Bumping this to alert those reading it that I'll be doing another cycle of new links in order to integrate global changes I made to accommodate the WoD -&gt; Chronicles of Darkness rebranding. Expect whatever links you're using now to stop working 24 hours from now. I'll update the three posts I've made with the link to use the new link then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T08:46:04-08:00","id":801425,"title":"","content":"Giving this topic a bump to announce that the rough draft of Alien: the Stranded is finished. Feel free to leave comments here. Those wishing to add remarks to the manuscript itself should PM me and I'll provide you with the &quot;commenting&quot; link (not doing that here to avoid spam bots). I'll be playtesting it come February (and going through March/April) but I'm not very likely to make any revisions before next Fall (or possibly next year -- among other things I want to write another novel and I've a pesky dissertation proposal that needs development).<br /> <br /> Feedback is welcome and muchly appreciated. If you can be specific as to where you perceive failings to be and suggest alternatives that would be best. The link again is: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fPVMwMZdnrJZiJkUVIYKCHTQnfmq0fiLqUhlLBGif4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T09:54:00-08:00","id":801467,"title":"","content":"Off World Supporters needs a system connected to it - otherwise, there's no point taking more than one dot.<br /> <br /> Also, you left out the electricity resistance in the Resistances section (or left <i>in</i> a reference in Electrocytes), and <i>really</i> need to condense the Conditions. They are all pretty wordy and (especially in the case of the Paranoia conditions) are kinda piddly in terms of modifiers. Good conditions have a small number of modifiers but communicate their effects through manipulating other mechanics.<br /> <br /> In general, it's fine to leave the Beat and Resolution triggers as sentence fragments. Compare:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Feverish [Condition]</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your character has contracted a disease that is making it gravely ill. Any time your character engages in combat, it suffers from the Sick (Grave) Tilt. More-over, when outside of combat, it must roll its Stamina + Resolve every time a number of hours equal to its Stamina have passed. On a failed roll it suffers one point of Bashing Damage. </span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> The character cannot heal damage while it suffers from this condition. If any lethal damage is suffered because of this condition, the character\u2019s sickness will worsen (see below). </span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Resolution:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> This condition may be resolved in one of four ways:</span></span></span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gain a beat and resolve this condition if a point of lethal damage is caused by it. The character gains the Delirious Condition. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gain a beat and resolve this condition after a number of days equal to the character\u2019s Stamina. The character gains the Delirious Condition.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gain a beat and resolve this condition if the character rolls an exceptional success on any roll to resist damage caused by the illness. The character gains the Recovering Condition.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gain a (single) beat if the character treats the sickness with medicine or by seeking treatment from a knowledgeable physician of some kind. Treatment requires medicinal substances of some kind which may have to be gathered (at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion). The character treating the disease makes an extended roll using Intelligence + Medicine. They must accumulate a number of successes equal to 15 - the sick character\u2019s Stamina. A failed roll represents an adverse reaction to the medication causing the sick character to suffer their Stamina in points of bashing damage. Once enough successes have been accumulated the Feverish Condition is resolved and sick character gains the Recovering Condition. In the event of a dramatic failure, the Feverish Condition is resolved and the sick character gains the Delirious Condition.</span></span></span></li> </ol> </div> </div> </div>to<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Feverish [Condition]</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your character has contracted a disease that is making it gravely ill. Any time your character engages in combat, it suffers from the Sick (Grave) Tilt. More-over, when outside of combat, it must roll its Stamina + Resolve every time a number of hours equal to its Stamina have passed. On a failed roll it suffers one point of Bashing Damage. </span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> The character cannot heal damage while it suffers from this condition. If a number of days equal to your Stamina pass or the damage from this conditions wraps around to Lethal, resolve this Condition and gain the Delirious Condition. Otherwise, you gain the Recovering Condition upon resolving this one.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Resolution:</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Get an Exceptional Success on the roll to prevent further damage. Someone scores [15 - your Stamina] successes on an extended Intelligence + Medicine roll.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Receive medical treatment from a professional.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally go even further than that and remove the need for an extended Medicine roll. I'd drop the Beat line and replace the Resolution line with:<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Resolution:</b> Get an Exceptional Success on the roll to prevent further damage. Receive professional medical treatment.<br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't swap between second and third persons like you do in the Condition; either stick with using you or your, or use it the whole way through.<br /> <hr /><br /> Remember, brevity is a virtue. I can't think of any official Conditions that I wouldn't be able to fit on one side of an index card.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:10:22-08:00","id":806381,"title":"","content":"Starting to read <b>Alien The Stranded</b> corebook and I like most what I see. It would be interesting experience to play a game in what you play a part of alien who plays a part to look human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For more useful comment, I just read section on using Latin as game terms and I maybe have something to add to it - <b>Seeing how Lating is seen as &quot;noble language&quot;, in that most modern Western dialects are diverted from, and Latin was spoken as language of Roman Empire - maybe Aliens like to use it, seeing Latin as &quot;highest of natives tongues&quot;, remembering partially high culture of their homeworld, now more and more eludes them as they are more Stranded on Earth.</b> Seeing the natural parallels with Latin as language is fairly obvious I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or you can even go full <a href=\"http://stargate.wikia.com/wiki/Ancient_language\" target=\"_blank\">Star Gate on that and say that Latin was based on speech of alien civilization</a>, so it's pointing Stranded they can build something on Earth, if they try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:23:31-08:00","id":809432,"title":"","content":"I now need only the conspiracy of Stranded, working inside the Earths governments, <b>X Files</b> style. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Could I make it with Alien game as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:19:35-08:00","id":809597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=809432#post809432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now need only the conspiracy of Stranded, working inside the Earths governments, <b>X Files</b> style. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Could I make it with Alien game as it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be able to. There is an entire appendix devoted to mortal collaborators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T00:40:07-08:00","id":812426,"title":"","content":"One kind of alien that I wish was covered, but isn't \u2014 though I mostly understand why:<br /> <br /> \u2022 \u201chumans from the stars\u201d: just as there are numerous alien races within each Taxon, wouldn't humanity itself be but one race within a Taxon? That is, this Taxon would involve species who could pass for human with at most a mundane disguise kit. The flip side of this is that they're unlikely to have Adaptations, and their lack of a means of Camouflage makes Exposure particularly problematic. They'd still be aliens though, with the usual susceptibility to Terran diseases, issues with Assimilation, and alien Vessels. This Taxon is the stereotypical <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordic_aliens\" target=\"_blank\">nordic alien</a> \u2014 though in typical Chronicles of Darkness fashion, they come in a variety of appearances rather than all conforming to a single human ethnicity. <br /> <br /> Other thoughts:<br /> \u2022 Shared Vessels: as written, <b>Alien: the Stranded</b> assumes that each alien has his, her, or its own Vessel. But what about spacecraft that had crew and/or passengers, not just a single occupant? This strikes me as a <i>frequent</i> occurrence, and one way to establish a tightly-knit Cluster of aliens \u2014 though the shared origin would tend to imply (but not mandate) a common Taxon and Occup\u0101tio as well. It would also tend to strain the Vessel's resources. <br /> <br /> \u2022 You need a Glossary of all the Latin terms you've used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T07:36:54-08:00","id":812590,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It needs a thorough indexing too. <br /> <br /> Regarding the &quot;humans from the stars&quot;, I was thinking that the Visiones could fulfill that role. The manifestation rules are actually pretty helpful in this case. <br /> <br /> However building them as using the exotic taxa rules would also make sense. Since they don't have a use for a camouflage adaptation, replacing it with a dread power would serve to differentiate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:13:28-08:00","id":818437,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Assimilation&quot; Is a bit too mixed a bag, power traits can have side effects but morality In my opinion holding to strict rules should be its own punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:54:16-08:00","id":818527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=818437#post818437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;Assimilation&quot; Is a bit too mixed a bag, power traits can have side effects but morality In my opinion holding to strict rules should be its own punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure I understand. Could you provide a bit more explanation regarding what you mean by &quot;mixed bag&quot;? The intent is that as aliens become more &quot;human&quot; their technology becomes more difficult for them to wield whereas it's harder for them to interact with humans when they are closer to their &quot;natural&quot; state. Like most of the &quot;morality&quot; analogues, the purpose isn't really to remark on their morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":"02-01-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T18:14:58-08:00","id":820667,"title":"","content":"This is really cool. It would be interesting to run a crossover game with an alien and something else. I could see aliens and Prometheans getting along. Or maybe trying to kill each other. It works both ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:49:09-08:00","id":821615,"title":"","content":"So my players have requested a &quot;custom&quot; character sheet for our playtest. I thought I would share it here for anyone else who's playing around with this ruleset. The 2-page sheet can be found at: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7vdpwhAJGx8bmotRFZxZk9LU1U/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7v...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> The template it uses is courtesy our very own Mr. Gone (thanks again Mr. Gone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:25:22-07:00","id":846599,"title":"","content":"Thread necromancy to let those using the old links know that I've updated the manuscript based on playtest results over the last month and a half. Mostly nerfed sickness die rolls, buffed armor effects, and clarified when to check for sickness (there's now a table). Also added in brief mechanics in the ST chapter about shared Vessel traits (the text was already 90% there). Toying with the idea of adding in Dataweaver's &quot;human&quot; aliens as another Exotic Taxa example / antagonist. The new link is: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fPVMwMZdnrJZiJkUVIYKCHTQnfmq0fiLqUhlLBGif4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I've updated the other links in this thread but am not going through the additional thread necromancy update the one other reference that I know is floating around somewhere here.<br /> <br /> Note for those who've bookmarked the old link. Update to the new link because the old one is going away sometime next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:24:49-07:00","id":944891,"title":"","content":"New version uploaded integrating lessons learned from actual gameplay. Most changes have to do with shared Vessels. Still no index and still no revision of text to improve pithiness of presentation. New link is here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fPVMwMZdnrJZiJkUVIYKCHTQnfmq0fiLqUhlLBGif4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Comments welcome but as I'm now working on my dissertation it will be a long while before additional revisions are made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:13:08-07:00","id":1400222,"title":"","content":"You know, thinking about it, and after giving the rulebook a light-ish/medium-ish skim, I think that it makes sense that the Stranded don't have a 'true' Power Stat like Blood Potency for Vampires, Satiety for Beasts or Primum for Demons since, ya' know, the Stranded are biological (usually), \u2018muggle\u2019 beings from another planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 07-08-2020, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T18:45:12-07:00","id":1401588,"title":"","content":"Yes, I've been toying with reworking their supernatural tolerance trait into a shared stat since it's meant to be representative of their (only partially operational) spacecraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T06:43:54-07:00","id":1401671,"title":"","content":"How to explain Vessel 10 not making it space worthy again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T09:04:38-07:00","id":1401702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1401671#post1401671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to explain Vessel 10 not making it space worthy again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it\u2019s been fully <i>fixed</i> doesn\u2019t automatically mean that it\u2019s been fully <i>refuelled</i>. I mean, is a car fully operational when it has an empty fuel tank, but everything else is in order?<br /> <br /> Possible solution; after reaching Vessel 10, the craft needs to have a full set of fuel tanks, the Stranded need to carefully extricate themselves from the local population and an extended roll (or a series of such rolls) needs to be beaten to properly get the ship out of the Earth\u2019s atmosphere and into N-Space at the correct velocity in the correct direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:32:11-07:00","id":1401723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1401671#post1401671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to explain Vessel 10 not making it space worthy again?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As TerrorCooper mentions above but also, the text descriptions are intended to provide storytellers with the latitude to make up excuses for why a Vessel 10 spacecraft may or may not be spaceworthy (and among these is that it might simply lack the facility for movement). It's left to individual troupes to explore what they want to vis-a-vis other worlds. The other point I think to make, is that the players' characters might have been marooned by their peers and, rather like the 7th, 8th, 9th, and part of the 10th season of Dr. Who (the Pertwee years if you're old enough to remember them), the players' characters might be stuck on Earth because the powers-that-be want it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T04:48:25-07:00","id":1401891,"title":"","content":"The vis-avis bit also made me realise something; a Stranded could be, well, 'Stranded', because they're using earth as their home base betwen interplanetary, interstellar or even intergalactic adventures, and they'd be able to take people with them Doctor Who style as companions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T13:47:34-07:00","id":1402111,"title":"","content":"That was by design","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T16:16:50-07:00","id":1402136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1402111#post1402111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was by design</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh... Alrighty then! Of course, such people would have the Conditioned Merit by default, due to them interacting with extra-terrestrial beings on the (semi-)regular.<br /> <br /> Also, just remembered; what are the Stranded's Stereotypes for Fan-Made Game lines, such as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\">Monarchs</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/PrincessTheHopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Nobles</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/HunchbackTheLurching\" target=\"_blank\">Miserable</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/GeniusTheTransgression\" target=\"_blank\">Genii</a>, etc and vice versa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T10:54:39-07:00","id":1403688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1402136#post1402136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... Alrighty then! Of course, such people would have the Conditioned Merit by default, due to them interacting with extra-terrestrial beings on the (semi-)regular.<br /> <br /> Also, just remembered; what are the Stranded's Stereotypes for Fan-Made Game lines, such as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\">Monarchs</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/PrincessTheHopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Nobles</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/HunchbackTheLurching\" target=\"_blank\">Miserable</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/GeniusTheTransgression\" target=\"_blank\">Genii</a>, etc and vice versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's one of the things Conditioned was designed to model.<br /> <br /> I never really consider how it would fit in with other fan-games. TBH, the only one of them that holds much appeal to me personally is Genius but, that has to do with how iconic I think mad scientists are to the horror genre (honestly, I really hope the next CoD game from OPP is for one of the big three iconics -- aliens, mad scientists, or zombies).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T15:34:14-07:00","id":1403896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1403688#post1403688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. That's one of the things Conditioned was designed to model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... really? Never thought of it. *shrug* Oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1403688#post1403688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really consider how it would fit in with other fan-games. TBH, the only one of them that holds much appeal to me personally is Genius but, that has to do with how iconic I think mad scientists are to the horror genre</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, then just leave it to the rest of us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1403688#post1403688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(honestly, I really hope the next CoD game from OPP is for one of the big three iconics -- aliens, mad scientists, or zombies).</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean <i>besides </i>Vampires, Werewolves and Magic-Users-of-Various-Stripes, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:36:24-07:00","id":1403992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1403896#post1403896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean <i>besides </i>Vampires, Werewolves and Magic-Users-of-Various-Stripes, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, Vampires, Werewolves, Promethean Monsters, Changelings, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:35:26-07:00","id":1404090,"title":"","content":"Well, if they <i>do</i> wind up doing game-lines of those three, then I hope that they take inspiration for each from here, G;tT and the OWoD fan-made game-line Zombie: the Coil (<a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Zombie:_The_Coil\" target=\"_blank\">https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Zombie:_The_Coil</a>) respectively.<br /> <br /> Also, since your actually interested in the Inspired, what sort of Stereotypes would <i>you</i> say that the Stranded hold towards them (at least in terms of those \u2018in the know\u2019 about them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T10:20:05-07:00","id":1404938,"title":"","content":"IIRC, I wrote the stereotypes from the perspective of the other splats and not the Aliens (I think Vampires don't even believe in Aliens). I would say that Geniuses are likely interested in dissecting or experimenting with Aliens but are somewhat dubious that they're actually from other worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T12:11:32-07:00","id":1406481,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, <b>Deviant</b> is to mad scientists as <b>Geist</b> is to ghosts: the protagonists aren't mad scientists, but rather the product of mad science \u2014 bearing in mind that a human trying to understand and make something with supernatural phenomena counts as \u201cmad science\u201d. <br /> <br /> Or maybe I should phrase that as \u201cmad science is to Deviants as alchemy is to Prometheans\u201d. <br /> <br /> So that just leaves aliens and zombies. <br /> <br /> But back to the Stranded: have you considered fancying the presentation up with fonts and images and putting it in the form of a PDF?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T15:15:01-07:00","id":1406517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/754554-alien-the-stranded?p=1404938#post1404938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, I wrote the stereotypes from the perspective of the other splats and not the Aliens (I think Vampires don't even believe in Aliens). I would say that Geniuses are likely interested in dissecting or experimenting with Aliens but are somewhat dubious that they're actually from other worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>To respond to each of the G:tT parts in order;<br /> <br /> As to be expected of them. Who knows just what sort of impossible Wonders they could conceive of after studying the Stranded's physiology, morphology, genetics, prosthetics, cybernetics and so on.<br /> <br /> Probably a lot less so in regards to those Genii who managed to explore far enough into space and return.<br /> <br /> Still, the Inspired would probably be the biggest mind screw one of the Stranded could encounter because the former is <i>clearly</i> making use of a strange, twisted form of alien (from the latter's perspective) science that blatantly follows some sort of insane code of logic, but the laws and rules are completely nonsensical and rarely exist outside of a limited radius around the Genius in question.<br /> <br /> Heck, the Genii literally <i>warp reality</i> in their immediate surroundings/vicinity to match how they believe reality functions, out of the sheer supernatural weight of their belief and madness/insanity! And if the finer details in the Genius' scientific worldview are sufficiently different, then a Stranded's Ornamenta could, at least theoretically, start developing bugs, defects, design flaws, etc or just become entirely non-functional.<br /> <br /> Just, imagine how terrifying and scary a fight against a High-Inspiration Genius could be for even the most prepared of the Stranded. Even moreso if it's a Collaboration of Genii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 08-05-2020, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T04:48:56-07:00","id":1481360,"title":"","content":"I would like to know, has anyone continued developing this project? Because i think it was actually very cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-22T02:12:10-08:00","id":1546279,"title":"","content":"Is this gameline dead ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.